+/* TAPE ECHO (Dark Funk Durcal): the delay as a three-head tape loop (the spring-and-tape echoes of the 70s). MENU-free:
+ * the FX family's TAPE ECHO page, G_DRLVL (HEADS: OFF H1 H2 H3 H1+2 H2+3 H1+3 ALL) and G_DRREV (WOW 0..127: wow, flutter
+ * and tape saturation). HEADS OFF: the delay bit for bit as before. The heads at TIME x1 x2 x3 (the 3 limited to the
+ * line), read between samples while the wow (~0.6 Hz) and the flutter (~6 Hz) move the tape; the repeats come back
+ * through the low-pass COLOR, a ~150 Hz high-pass (the thin tape) and a soft saturation, so a high FDBK self-oscillates
+ * but stays bounded (the line is int16, the sum is the mean of the heads) */
